==Trivia==
*Although Noodle Nirvana is a ramen-themed sub-chapter, its Japanese name strangely spells ''ramen'' as ラメン ''ramen'', whereas the Japanese word for ramen is ラーメン ''rāmen'', which has a ''[[wikipedia:Chōonpu|chōonpu]]'' (ー).
*[[Mass-Chashu-Sets]] is a pun on ''[[wikipedia:Massachusetts|Massachusetts]]'' and チャーシュー ''chā shū'' ([[wikipedia:char siu|char siu]]). Its Japanese name, Torori Chā-shū (トロリチャー州, "Melty Char Province"), combines チャーシュー ''chā shū'' with 州 ''shū'' (province).
*[[Golden Gate Menma]] is named after the [[wikipedia:Golden Gate Bridge|Golden Gate Bridge]] and [[wikipedia:Menma|menma]], a condiment consisting of bamboo shoots fermented in lactic acid.
*[[Kernel Chaos]]'s Japanese name, Konton Kōn Zōn (混沌コーンゾーン, "Chaos Corn Zone"), may play off of how 混沌 (chaos) and 渾沌 (steamed [[wikipedia:Manjū|manjū]] or steamed mochi) are both read as ''konton''.
*[[Fishcake Fortress]]'s Japanese name, Narū-tō, (ナルー塔, "Naru Tower") is derived from ''[[wikipedia:Narutomaki|narutomaki]]'', a common ramen topping consisting of ''[[wikipedia:Surimi|surimi]]'' with a pink spiral pattern. It may also reference [[wikipedia:ja:鳴門わかめ|Naruto wakame]] (edible [[wikipedia:Wakame|wakame]] harvested from around [[wikipedia:Naruto, Tokushima|Naruto, Tokushima]]) or the manga ''[[wikipedia:Naruto|Naruto]]'', whose eponymous [[wikia:naruto:Naruto Uzumaki|protagonist]] loves to eat ramen.
*[[Bowl of Bliss]]'s Japanese name, Ippai no Shiawase (一杯の幸せ, "Containerful of Happiness"; 一杯 can mean a bowlful, cupful, spoonful, etc.), may be a reference to ''[[wikipedia:ja:スプーン一杯の幸せ|Spoon Ippai no Shiawase]]'' (スプーン一杯の幸せ, "Spoonful of Happiness"), a series of novels by [[wikipedia:Keiko Ochiai|Keiko Ochiai]] that was adapted into a film starring [[wikipedia:Junko Sakurada|Junko Sakurada]]. ''Spoon Ippai no Shiawase'' is also the name of Sakurada's [[wikia:jpop:Spoon Ippai no Shiawase|fourth album]], which includes the film's theme song, "Hitori Aruki".
*Noodle Nirvana having [[Inumusha]] and the [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]] may be because they debuted in [[Walk of Fame]], the 37th [[Stories of Legend]] sub-chapter.

